---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals build manufacturing or production management software?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Custom systems can be designed around production orders, stages, inventory, purchasing, approvals, reporting and other agreed operational requirements.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can manufacturing software integrate with accounting, CRM or ecommerce systems?",
    answer:
      "Where suitable APIs or supported integration mechanisms exist, operational systems can be connected to reduce duplicate data entry and improve continuity.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can inventory and production be managed in the same system?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Depending on the workflow, materials, work orders, consumption, finished goods and related movements can be designed into one connected system.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can production alerts or approvals be automated?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Predictable alerts, approvals and status-driven actions can often be automated once the manufacturing rules are clearly defined.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can dashboards show production and stock performance?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Reporting can be developed around available data such as production status, stock levels, purchasing, order progress and other operational KPIs.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you have to replace our existing ERP?",
    answer:
      "No. Replacement is only one option. Existing systems may be extended, integrated or complemented with additional software where that is operationally more sensible.",
  },
];
---

<section class="manufacturing-faq">
  <div class="site-container manufacturing-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Manufacturing FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions to answer before replacing another production spreadsheet.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="manufacturing-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .manufacturing-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .manufacturing-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(17rem, 0.7fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .manufacturing-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .manufacturing-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .manufacturing-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .manufacturing-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .manufacturing-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .manufacturing-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .manufacturing-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
